cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this DTTS addendum package, cite the repository archive and preserve the medical non-claim boundary. Zenodo identifiers for this repository are repository-archive DOIs, not standalone peer-reviewed article DOIs."
type: software
title: "DTTS v0.3.0: Claim-Bounded Threshold, Hysteresis, and Rescue-Regime Audits for a Sleep-Like Recovery-Transition Toy Network"
authors:
  - family-names: "Yoshimura"
    given-names: "Keiji"
    affiliation: "Independent Researcher"
version: "v0.3.0-synthesis-addendum-source-license-checked"
date-released: "2026-05-25"
url: "https://github.com/yokken0907/dynamical-threshold-theory-of-sleep"
repository-code: "https://github.com/yokken0907/dynamical-threshold-theory-of-sleep"
abstract: "Claim-bounded synthesis addendum for DTTS toy-model audits of sleep-like recovery transitions in finite adaptive networks. The package reports threshold-like sleep-gate onset, hysteresis-like persistence, structurally aligned selective protection, perturbation-recovery response, topology/noise robustness, failure boundaries, and frozen rescue-policy holdout behavior within tested toy-model regimes. It does not claim clinical sleep diagnosis, medical advice, treatment guidance, human or animal sleep-data validation, EEG or wearable-device prediction, or a complete biological theory of sleep."
keywords:
  - DTTS
  - sleep-like recovery transition
  - adaptive networks
  - threshold dynamics
  - hysteresis
  - selective protection
  - toy model
  - claim boundary
  - evidence-led protocol
